    "checkpointCrashResidueCleanup": "authenticated checkpoint ownership-journal prefixes authorize only identity-and-content-matched stage-ready temp/final states: stage-ready accepts temp-only, the exact two-link alias pair, or final-only; link-observed accepts the exact pair or final-only; published accepts final-only. Recovery first opens the journal O_NOFOLLOW, authenticates its complete canonical bytes/full identity/content/nlink, and holds that descriptor plus the authenticated checkpoint descriptor across all exact alias and journal unlinks and root fsync before finally closing them. Missing, empty, torn-to-empty, intent-only, drifted, externally linked, unknown-sibling, reader-close-uncertain, factory-cleanup-uncertain, or otherwise unauthenticated residues are preserved and RED_QUARANTINED; a zero-valid-prefix torn journal with any checkpoint residue is classified before repair and is never truncated; normal success removes the exact ownership journal and leaves the committed final unclaimed by cleanup",
